            "error",
            {
                "object": "JSON",
                "property": "parse",
                "message": "`JSON.parse` returns `any`, and that `any` flows unchecked into every read downstream, which is where most no-unsafe findings come from. Parse through @nexus/source/structured-text/json/Json instead: `parseJsonOrThrow(text, context, isValue)` with a guard from @nexus/source/validation/Guard when the code reads fields, or `parseJson(text, context)` and handle its 'Invalid' outcome where bad input already falls back. Name the source in `context`. For a deep clone, use `structuredClone`."
            }
